        "locator": "opening",
        "quote": "In the model a choice is that kind of settling, the same way every run."
      },
      {
        "source": "d256279f-196b-4be6-a8ef-47554d1d19b0",
        "locator": "What this answers",
        "quote": "The model gives it a mechanism: choice as deterministic settling, freedom as measured irreducibility."
      },
      {
        "source": "d256279f-196b-4be6-a8ef-47554d1d19b0",
        "locator": "A choice as settling",
        "quote": "A different self under the same urge settles elsewhere, so the self’s own structure is a cause of the choice and not a channel for the urge."
      },
      {
        "source": "d256279f-196b-4be6-a8ef-47554d1d19b0",
        "locator": "Determined, not predestined",
        "quote": "The future is fixed and still has to be lived to be known."
